1
00:00:00,598 --> 00:00:02,768
(Howard:)Nine rings were made
for use in the movies.

2
00:00:02,933 --> 00:00:06,643
(Howard:)Three were given to members
of the cast. The rest were destroyed.

3
00:00:07,021 --> 00:00:08,311
(Howard:)Except one.

4
00:00:08,481 --> 00:00:11,321
(Howard:)One was stolen.

5
00:00:11,609 --> 00:00:16,609
(Howard:)Gentlemen, this is the One Ring.

6
00:00:19,825 --> 00:00:21,455
(Howard:)Mine.

7
00:00:23,037 --> 00:00:25,827
(Leonard:)No, it is not yours.
We all went in on the box together.

8
00:00:25,998 --> 00:00:27,958
(Sheldon:)Yes, but I found it in the box.

9
00:00:28,125 --> 00:00:30,465
(Sheldon:)And the laws of maritime salvage
clearly state...

10
00:00:30,628 --> 00:00:33,718
(Sheldon:)...that the finder of a sunken treasure
is the owner.

11
00:00:33,881 --> 00:00:35,711
(Leonard:)How is this maritime salvage?

12
00:00:35,883 --> 00:00:38,173
(Sheldon:)Other than the lack of water,
how is it not?

13
00:00:38,344 --> 00:00:40,674
(Raj:)Wait, Sheldon.
Stop being crazy for a second.

14
00:00:41,013 --> 00:00:42,843
(Raj:)How much is something like this worth?

15
00:00:43,015 --> 00:00:45,355
(Howard:)Well, it's tough to say, since it's hot.

16
00:00:45,518 --> 00:00:47,518
(Howard:)On the underground market,
my guy figures--

17
00:00:47,686 --> 00:00:50,646
(Raj:)-Your guy Eddie Crispo?
-Yes.

18
00:00:53,150 --> 00:00:57,860
-He figures 10-, maybe 15,000.
-Okay, that's a lot of money.

19
00:00:58,030 --> 00:01:01,370
(Raj:)The wise thing to do
is invest it in something practical.

